                    <p>
                        These Terms of Service govern your use of the
                        <strong>WashFlow Carwash Management System</strong>
                        operated by WashFlow ("we", "our", "the platform")
                        accessible at <strong>splashcity.store</strong>.
                        By logging into and using this system you agree
                        to these terms in full.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <!-- DEFINITIONS -->
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">Definitions</h5>
                    <p>
                        <strong>"System"</strong> refers to the WashFlow
                        Carwash Management System.<br />
                        <strong>"User"</strong> refers to any authorised
                        staff member accessing the system.<br />
                        <strong>"Business"</strong> refers to the carwash
                        subscribing to and using WashFlow.<br />
                        <strong>"WashFlow"</strong> refers to the platform
                        provider and software owner.<br />
                        <strong>"Subscription"</strong> refers to the
                        monthly recurring access agreement.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">1. Acceptance of Terms</h5>
                    <p>
                        By accessing and using this system you confirm that
                        you are an authorised staff member and that you agree
                        to comply with these terms fully.
                        Unauthorised access is strictly prohibited.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">2. User Accounts</h5>
                    <ul class="mb-4">
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            Each staff member is issued a personal account.
                            You are responsible for all activity under
                            your account.
                        </li>
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            You must never share your login credentials
                            with any other person.
                        </li>
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            You must log out at the end of every shift.
                        </li>
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            You must notify your administrator immediately
                            if you believe your account has been compromised.
                        </li>
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            Accounts are non-transferable and remain the
                            property of the business.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">3. Acceptable Use</h5>
                    <p>You agree to use this system only for its intended purpose. You must not:</p>
                    <ul class="mb-4">
                        <li class="mb-2">Access, modify, or delete records you are not authorised to change</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Attempt to access another staff member's account</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Export or share customer data outside the business without authorisation</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Use the system to process fraudulent transactions</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Attempt to circumvent security controls or role-based permissions</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Introduce malware, viruses, or harmful code into the system</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">4. Role-Based Access</h5>
                    <p>
                        Access to features and data is restricted based on
                        user roles assigned by the Administrator. You must
                        not attempt to access features or data outside your
                        assigned permissions. Role assignments are controlled
                        by the business owner and WashFlow administrators.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">5. Data Accuracy</h5>
                    <p>
                        You are responsible for the accuracy of data you
                        enter. This includes customer details, transaction
                        amounts, payment methods, and M-Pesa codes.
                        Deliberately entering false or misleading information
                        is a serious breach of these terms.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">6. Billing & Financial Responsibility</h5>
                    <p>
                        All transactions recorded must accurately reflect
                        services rendered and payments received including
                        cash, M-Pesa, and card payments.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="mb-4">
                        <li class="mb-2">All amounts must be verified correct before completing a transaction</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Recorded transactions form official business records and must not be altered without proper authorisation</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Errors or discrepancies must be reported immediately to a supervisor</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Processing fake, duplicate, or unauthorised transactions is strictly prohibited</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">7. Payment Verification</h5>
                    <p>
                        Users must ensure all digital payments including
                        M-Pesa are verified before completing a transaction.
                        The system records M-Pesa transaction reference codes
                        which must match the actual payment received.
                        Confirming payment without actual receipt of funds
                        is a disciplinary offence.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">8. Receipts and Records</h5>
                    <p>
                        All transactions generate permanent records used
                        for reporting, auditing, and reconciliation. Users
                        must ensure that transaction records match actual
                        services delivered and payments collected.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">9. Audit Trail</h5>
                    <p>
                        All actions in this system are logged and linked
                        to your account — transactions created, records
                        modified, and data exported. These logs may be
                        reviewed by management at any time. By using this
                        system you consent to this monitoring.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">10. Monitoring & Security Logs</h5>
                    <p>
                        The system monitors usage patterns and activity
                        to detect suspicious behaviour and ensure security
                        compliance in accordance with ISO 27001 standards.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">11. Confidentiality</h5>
                    <p>
                        All system data is confidential including customer
                        records, revenue figures, transaction history,
                        staff information, and expense data. You must not
                        disclose any of this information to persons outside
                        the business without express written authorisation.
                        This obligation continues after your employment ends.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">12. Intellectual Property</h5>
                    <p>
                        This system is powered by <strong>WashFlow</strong>
                        — a proprietary carwash management platform.
                        The software, design, and all associated intellectual
                        property remain the property of WashFlow. You are
                        granted a limited, non-exclusive licence to use the
                        system solely for operations within your business.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">13. System Availability</h5>
                    <p>
                        The system may be temporarily unavailable due to
                        maintenance, upgrades, or unexpected technical issues.
                        While we aim to ensure continuous availability,
                        we do not guarantee uninterrupted access at all times.
                        We are not liable for losses arising from system
                        downtime beyond our reasonable control.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">14. Data Backup</h5>
                    <p>
                        While reasonable measures are taken to protect and
                        back up data, WashFlow does not guarantee that data
                        will never be lost or corrupted due to unforeseen
                        technical failures. Users are encouraged to export
                        records regularly and report any issues promptly.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">15. Third-Party Services</h5>
                    <p>
                        This system relies on third-party services including
                        M-Pesa payment infrastructure (Safaricom), cloud
                        hosting providers, and SSL certificate providers.
                        WashFlow is not responsible for outages, failures,
                        or changes caused by these external services.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">16. Security Responsibilities</h5>
                    <p>
                        Users are responsible for maintaining the security
                        of their devices and ensuring that their login
                        credentials are not exposed or compromised.
                        Always log out on shared devices.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">17. Session Management</h5>
                    <p>
                        Sessions automatically expire after 8 hours of
                        inactivity. Users must log in again to continue
                        using the system. Always log out manually at the
                        end of your shift.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">18. Misuse of System</h5>
                    <p>
                        Any misuse of the system including fraud, data
                        manipulation, or unauthorised access may result
                        in immediate account suspension, disciplinary action,
                        termination of employment, and possible civil or
                        criminal legal action under Kenyan law.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">19. Termination of Access</h5>
                    <p>
                        Access may be suspended or terminated at any time
                        without notice if you breach these terms, your
                        employment ends, or management determines access
                        should be revoked. Upon termination you must
                        immediately cease use and must not attempt to
                        regain access.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <!-- SUBSCRIPTION SECTION -->
                    <div class="p-4 rounded mb-4"
                         style="background:#f0f7ff;border-left:4px solid #1565C0;">
                        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="color:#1565C0;">
                            20. Subscription & Billing
                        </h5>
                        <p>
                            Access to WashFlow is provided on a monthly
                            subscription basis. The subscribing business
                            agrees to pay the applicable recurring fee
                            for continued access.
                        </p>
                        <ul class="mb-3">
                            <li class="mb-2">Subscription fees are billed monthly in advance</li>
                            <li class="mb-2">Payment is accepted via M-Pesa or as otherwise agreed</li>
                            <li class="mb-2">Failure to pay by the due date may result in suspension of access</li>
                            <li class="mb-2">Access is restored once all outstanding payments are cleared</li>
                            <li class="mb-2">Subscription fees are subject to change with 30 days prior notice</li>
                            <li class="mb-2">Continued use of the system constitutes acceptance of applicable charges</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">21. Suspension for Non-Payment</h5>
                    <p>
                        WashFlow reserves the right to suspend or restrict
                        access to the system if subscription payments are
                        overdue by more than 7 days. This may include
                        restricting access to dashboards, reports, new wash
                        processing, and transaction features until full
                        payment is received.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">22. Data Retention After Non-Payment</h5>
                    <p>
                        In the event of non-payment, business data will be
                        retained for a period of 30 days after suspension.
                        Continued failure to settle outstanding balances
                        beyond this period may result in permanent deletion
                        of all system data. WashFlow is not liable for
                        data loss resulting from non-payment.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">23. Refund Policy</h5>
                    <p>
                        Subscription fees are non-refundable once access
                        to the system has been granted for the billing period,
                        except where required by Kenyan consumer protection law.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">24. Limitation of Liability</h5>
                    <p>
                        WashFlow's total liability for any claim arising
                        from use of the system shall not exceed the total
                        subscription fees paid in the preceding 3 months.
                        We are not liable for indirect losses, lost profits,
                        or business interruption.
                    </p>
                    <hr class="my-4" />
